cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this report, please cite it as below."
type: report
title: "Engineering Principles for Auditable Long-Term Memory in Companion Agents"
abstract: >-
  A technical report on rebuilding the long-term memory of a single-user
  companion agent around five engineering invariants: a single write path,
  a single retrieval path, measured (not asserted) thresholds,
  direction-asserted ranking terms, and a startup auditor that detects
  un-migrated existing data. Includes empirical results on a 26-query
  golden set and an anytime-valid betting confidence sequence replacing
  rolling-window intervals for streaming monitors.
authors:
